A towering, serpentine dragon made entirely of tangled code and glowing characters—half Latin alphabet, half Japanese kanji and Chinese hanzi—coiling through a misty bamboo forest. The dragon's body is impossibly long and convoluted, stretching endlessly into fog, while beside it floats a small, elegant origami crane formed from clean, minimal folded paper with just a few precise creases. Style of Piet Mondrian: the dragon constructed from chaotic intersecting black lines and blocks of primary red, yellow, and blue, while the crane is rendered in pure white with single bold geometric segments. The contrast between overwhelming complexity and refined simplicity dominates the composition, with the forest rendered as vertical black lines against cream background.
